@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each positional object to a string, joins them with ``sep`` and writes them followed by ``end``. It does not pretty-print, wrap, crop, process markup or replace emoji codes, so the output is exactly the raw text. It does apply a basic ``style`` and automatic highlighting (controlled by the ``highlight`` parameter, which defaults to ``True``)::
+
+    >>> console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ")
+
+Use ``out`` when you want predictable plain text output and do not need rich formatting.
+
+
